assification at time of detection. During the twelve months ended May 31, 2026, Abnormal detected an average normalized volume of \u003e1,200 attacks per 1,000 mailboxes that bypassed Secure Email Gateways each month, considering attack volume bypassing any Secure Email Gateway across all Abnormal customers. Supported by Abnormal Threat Intelligence research documenting attacks other solutions could not detect; Gartner, Overcome AI-Powered Attacks by Leveling Up Your Email Security Platform, Nikul Patel, Deepak Mishra, Max Taggett, June 19 2025 (“SEG solutions face limitations in detection efficacy”); The Forrester Wave™: Email, Messaging, And Collaboration Security Solutions, Q2 2025 (Abnormal AI has been named a Leader in The Forrester Wave™: Email, Messaging, And Collaboration Security Solutions, Q2 2025—among the ten vendors evaluated. Abnormal also received the highest score in the Strategy category, as well as the highest scores possible in the Vision, Innovation, and Roadmap criteria.); and Terrence Williams. (2025). “2025 SANS Detection Engineering Survey: Evolving Practices in Modern Security Operations.” SANS Institute (67% of organizations rely on behavior-based detection over traditional signature-based methods). Individual security outcomes may vary.1d:T56f,Based on Abnormal internal benchmarking, March 1, 2026 – June 23, 2026. We compared Abnormal’s purpose-built behavioral detection system with seven general-purpose large language models—Claude Opus 4.8, Claude Opus 4.6, Claude Sonnet 4.5, Claude Haiku 4.5, GPT-4.1, GPT-5 Mini, and Gemini 3.5 Flash—each run as a single-pass email classifier under detection-oriented prompting, evaluated against two balanced sets of 1,000 real production messages each — 1,000 confirmed attacks and 1,000 confirmed-safe samples, corpus design reviewed by the Abnormal Detection team, scored against expert human review by Abnormal threat analysts whose judgments are the reference standard throughout. Detection, cost, and speed were selected as the primary measures of security effectiveness and operational efficiency for enterprise email threat detection. Cost and latency figures are p50 (median) measurements from the runs and are not sensitive to dataset composition, prompt, or configuration. Detection figures reflect a focused evaluation set and are illustrative of this test rather than a guarantee of production results, which vary by environment and over time. LLM results depend on prompt and configuration; multiples are relative to the specific models and settings shown. Claude, GPT, and Gemini are trademarks of their respective owners; comparisons are for informational purposes.14:[\"$\",\"$L1b\",null,{\"formats\":\"$undefined\",\"locale\":\"en\",\"messages\":{\"relatedResources\":{\"viewAllLabel\":\"View All Resources\"},\"ui\":{\"isc2CpeBadge\":\"ISC2 CPE\",\"faqHeading\":\"FAQ\",\"shareHeading\":\"Share\",\"youMayLikeHeading\":\"You may like\",\"learnMoreLabel\":\"Learn More\",\"speakersHeading\":\"Speakers\",\"claimIsc2CreditLabel\":\"Claim Your ISC2 Credit\",\"resourcesBreadcrumbLabel\":\"Resources\",\"resourceTypeLabels\":{\"analystResearch\":\"Analyst Research\",\"dataSheets\":\"Data Sheets\",\"productDemos\":\"Product Demos\",\"industryBriefs\":\"Industry Briefs\",\"podcasts\":\"Podcasts\",\"threatReports\":\"Threat Reports\",\"tools\":\"Tools\",\"videos\":\"Videos\",\"webinars\":\"Webinars\",\"whitePapers\":\"White Papers\"},\"resourceCpe\":{\"title\":\"Earn ISC2 CPE\",\"creditsBare\":\"credits\",\"creditsParenSingular\":\"({count} credit)\",\"creditsParenPlural\":\"({count} credits)\",\"hourlySingular\":\"After viewing this resource, you are eligible for {count} ISC2 CPE credit for each hour viewed\",\"hourlyPlural\":\"After viewing this resource, you are eligible for {count} ISC2 CPE credits for each hour viewed\",\"hourlyTotalSingular\":\", for a total of up to {count} credit\",\"hourlyTotalPlural\":\", for a total of up to {count} credits\",\"staticEligible\":\"This r