,\"summary\":\"New suite extends Abnormal’s behavioral security approach to give enterprises visibility and governance over their AI, control over the AI their employees use, and protection against AI-driven attacks\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/abnormal-ai-expands-its-ai-security-suite\"},{\"date\":\"Sep 8, 2026\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal AI Announces that SoftBank Corp. Begins Offering Its Enterprise Email Security Platform in Japan\",\"summary\":\"\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/abnormal-ai-announces-that-softbank-corp-begins-offering-its-enterprise-email-security-platform-in-japan\"},{\"date\":\"Sep 3, 2026\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal AI Brings OpenAI Daybreak Models Into AI Cloud Security to Protect Against Rogue AI\",\"summary\":\"Abnormal's new AI Cloud Security product enables enterprises to detect and respond to risky or malicious AI-agent behavior in cloud environments. Abnormal's behavioral AI platform delivers real-time anomaly detection with autonomous investigation and response, using OpenAI Daybreak models to power investigation.\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/abnormal-ai-brings-openai-daybreak-models-into-ai-cloud-security-to-protect-against-rogue-ai\"},{\"date\":\"Sep 1, 2026\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal AI Joins Project Watershed 250 to Strengthen Cybersecurity for Texas Water Utilities\",\"summary\":\"Abnormal will offer its AI-native email threat detection at no cost to participating water utilities across Texas.\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/abnormal-ai-joins-project-watershed-250-to-strengthen-cybersecurity-for-texas-water-utilities\"},{\"date\":\"Aug 26, 2026\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal AI Extends Its Email Security Platform Across Inbound, Outbound, and Human Layers of Email Risk\",\"summary\":\"New capabilities add customizable detection controls, outbound data-loss prevention, and adaptive phishing-simulation training to Abnormal's email security platform.\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/abnormal-expands-email-security-platform\"},{\"date\":\"Aug 19, 2026\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal AI and OpenAI Partner to Accelerate Secure Enterprise AI Adoption and Strengthen Cyber Defense\",\"summary\":\"Abnormal will expand its use of OpenAI across its products and business, while the companies collaborate on new capabilities that improve security outcomes and help enterprises accelerate the safe adoption of AI.\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/abnormal-openai-partnership\"},{\"date\":\"Aug 18, 2026\",\"headline\":\"IMDA Accreditation Expands Abnormal AI’s Opportunities Across Singapore's Public and Enterprise Sectors\",\"summary\":\"Abnormal Behavioural Security Platform recognised as a trusted solution for government and enterprise adoption\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/abnormal-earns-imda-accreditation\"},{\"date\":\"Aug 11, 2026\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal AI Pursues FedRAMP Class D (High) Certification\",\"summary\":\"Milestone builds on Abnormal's existing FedRAMP Class C (Moderate) certification, with Tennessee Valley Authority returning as agency sponsor for the second time\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/abnormal-pursues-fedramp-class-d-certification\"},{\"date\":\"Jul 28, 2026\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal AI Extends its Behavioral Security Platform to Identity and AI Security\",\"summary\":\"Abnormal launches three new products: Identity Threat Protection, AI Governance, and Infiltration Prevention to secure the modern identity attack surface.\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/abnormal-extends-behavioral-security-platform\"},{\"date\":\"May 19, 2026\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal AI Named to CNBC Disruptor 50 List for Third Consecutive Year\",\"summary\":\"The recognition reflects Abnormal's position at the forefront of AI-native cybersecurity, and a year of milestone product innovation, global expansion, and industry accolades\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/cnbc-disruptor-2026\"},{\"date\":\"Apr 29, 2026\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal AI Expands Leadership Team to Advance Behavioral AI Platform\",\"summary\":\"\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/abnormal-appoints-three-senior-execs\"},{\"date\":\"Apr 22, 2026\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal AI 2026 Attack Landscape Report: Threat Actors Move Beyond Technical Exploits to Target Human Behavior and Trusted Relationships\",\"summary\":\"New research shows that 61% of business email compromise is now vendor-related, as attackers increasingly mimic everyday workflows.\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/2026-attack-landscape-report\"},{\"date\":\"Mar 17, 2026\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal AI Delivers Behavioral Foundation Model to Combat the Era of AI-Driven Attacks\",\"summary\":\"Introducing Attune 1.0, the multimodal AI foundation that unifies identity, context, and content signals to prevent AI-driven attacks targeting the modern enterprise\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/announcing-attune-10\"},{\"date\":\"Dec 3, 2025\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal AI Named a Leader for the Second Consecutive Year in the 2025 Gartner® Magic Quadrant™ for Email Security\",\"summary\":\"Recognized for Completeness of Vision and Ability to Execute; Positioned Furthest on the Vision Axis for the Second Consecutive Year\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/announcing-2025-gartner-magic-quadrant-email-security-leader\"},{\"date\":\"Nov 4, 2025\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal AI Reveals the Growing Risk of Human Error in Enterprise Email\",\"summary\":\"98% of security leaders consider misdirected email a significant risk—surpassing even malware and credential theft\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/misdirected-email-prevention-survey\"},{\"date\":\"Sep 23, 2025\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal AI Achieves GovRAMP Authorization to Secure State, Local, and Educational Organizations\",\"summary\":\"GovRAMP authorization highlights customer trust in Abnormal to deliver AI-powered protection against the full spectrum of email-based threats\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/announcing-govramp-authorization\"},