vation in AI\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/account-takeover-protection-expansion\"},{\"date\":\"Mar 21, 2024\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal Security Expands Executive Team, Appoints Smita Sanadhya as Chief Financial Officer and Jeff True as Chief Legal Officer\",\"summary\":\"The two executives join Abnormal’s C-Suite as the email security leader enters next phase of growth.\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/cfo-clo-appointments\"},{\"date\":\"Feb 20, 2024\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal Security Commits to Federal Sector, Hires Industry Veteran James Yeager to Lead Sales Strategy\",\"summary\":\"Seasoned executive to drive strategic growth as costly email attacks inundate federal government\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/fed-expansion\"},{\"date\":\"Feb 6, 2024\",\"headline\":\"C-Suite Receives 42x More QR Code Attacks Than Average Employee, According to New Research from Abnormal Security\",\"summary\":\"Quishing is on the rise as a novel social engineering attack, while traditional social engineering attacks like BEC and VEC also continue to grow\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/h1-2024-threat-report\"},{\"date\":\"Jan 10, 2024\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal Security Expands Channel and Alliances Leadership, Appoints Jonathan Corini as VP of Worldwide Channel Sales and Stephanie Goodman as Head of Global Alliances\",\"summary\":\"The sales leaders join Abnormal as the company seeks to deepen existing relationships and expand global partnerships\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/channelgrowth\"},{\"date\":\"Jan 3, 2024\",\"headline\":\"Kevin O’Leary, Venture Capitalist and Shark, Keynotes Vision 2024, Sponsored by Abnormal Security\",\"summary\":\"Second Annual Vision Conference Will Explore 2024 Cyber Threats in the Age of AI\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/vision24\"},{\"date\":\"Nov 21, 2023\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal Security Named a Fortune AI 50 Innovator, Capping a Year of Notable AI Award Wins\",\"summary\":\"Abnormal Continues Its 2023 Track Record of Industry Recognition for Its AI-Native Cybersecurity Capabilities\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/fortune-ai-50\"},{\"date\":\"Nov 2, 2023\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal Security Announces Enhanced Capabilities to Detect QR Code Attacks, as Quishing Accounts for 17% of All Advanced Attacks\",\"summary\":\"Information Extracted from QR Codes Enhances Abnormal’s AI Detection Engine, Providing Increased Protection Against Evolving Email Attacks\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/qr-code-detector\"},{\"date\":\"Oct 24, 2023\",\"headline\":\"New Survey From Abnormal Security Reveals 98% Of Security Leaders Worry About the Risks of Generative AI\",\"summary\":\"Security leaders are highly concerned about generative AI’s potential to create more sophisticated email attacks—yet, many are unprepared to effectively protect against it\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/state-of-email-security-ai-powered-world\"},{\"date\":\"Sep 13, 2023\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal Security Launches Limited Web Series on the Convergence of AI + Cybersecurity, Featuring Kevin Poulsen and Zack Kass\",\"summary\":\"The series includes speakers from OpenAI, CrowdStrike, Arrow Electronics and GuidePoint Security to showcase how AI is changing cybersecurity\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/convergence\"},{\"date\":\"Aug 15, 2023\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal Security Crosses $100M in ARR in Four Years, Advancing Position as AI Leader in Cybersecurity\",\"summary\":\"AI-native company appoints cybersecurity veterans Michael DeCesare and Maya Marcus to executive team to fuel company’s hypergrowth\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/100m-arr-ai-leader-cybersecurity\"},{\"date\":\"Aug 10, 2023\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal Security Recognized as a Leader in AI, Cloud, and Cybersecurity by Industry and Customers Alike\",\"summary\":\"Abnormal Debuts on the Forbes Cloud 100 and Secures Additional Recognition from Redpoint Ventures, Bloomberg, Gartner Peer Insights, and CRN\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/q2-2023-awards-2\"},{\"date\":\"Aug 8, 2023\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal Announces New Capability to Detect AI-Generated Email Attacks\",\"summary\":\"New CheckGPT tool evaluates the likelihood of email attacks being created by generative AI chatbots including ChatGPT\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/checkgpt\"},{\"date\":\"Aug 2, 2023\",\"headline\":\"Average Organization Integrates 379 Third-Party Applications Into Email Environment, According to New Research From Abnormal Security\",\"summary\":\"Social engineering attacks also continue to grow, with BEC attacks increasing by 55% and nearly half of all organizations receiving at least one VEC attack since January\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/h2-2023-threat-report\"},{\"date\":\"Jun 21, 2023\",\"headline\":\"New Research from Abnormal Security Highlights 10X Increase in Business Email Compromise Attacks in Europe\",\"summary\":\"BEC continues to grow in Europe, with spike over the summer holidays\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/europe-bec-trends\"},{\"date\":\"May 9, 2023\",\"headline\":\"New Research from Abnormal Security Shows the Rise of Business Email Compromise Attacks Sent from Israel\",\"summary\":\"The report reveals how an emerging threat group employs a multi-phased BEC attack with an M\u0026amp;A theme to steal  from multinational enterprises\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/israel-bec-report\"},{\"date\":\"May 2, 2023\",\"headline\":\"New Survey from ESG Reveals Trends Shaping Communication and Collaboration Application Security\",\"summary\":\"More than two thirds of IT and security leaders are concerned that attackers are leveraging communication and collaboration channels beyond email to evade security controls\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/esg-survey\"},{\"date\":\"Apr 25, 2023\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal Security Expands Behavioral AI Platform to Protect Against Multi-Channel Attacks\",\"summary\":\"New Platform Enhancements Enable Detection of Email-like Attacks Across Slack, Microsoft Teams and Zoom\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/multichannel-attack-protection\"},{\"date\":\"Apr 13, 2023\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal Security Showcases AI Strength with Six Award Wins\",\"summary\":\"Abnormal Recognized by Forbes, Fast Company, the Cybersecurity Excellence Awards, and the Globee Cybersecurity Awards for its Behavioral AI Approach to Email Security\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/2023-awards-wins-2\"},{\"date\":\"Mar 29, 2023\",\"headline\":\"CrowdStrike Invests in Abnormal Security and Launches New Partnership to Stop Breaches by Combining the Power of Behavioral AI with Industry-Leading Next-Gen SIEM\",\"summary\":\"CrowdStrike Falcon Fund Investment to Help Drive Protection Across the Broader Attack Surface\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/crowdstrike-partnership\"},{\"date\":\"Feb 22, 2023\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal Security Named as a Representative Vendor in 2023 Gartner® Market Guide for Email Security\",\"summary\":\"Recommendations include using AI-based email security solutions that can detect communication patterns and conversational-style anomalies.\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/abnormal-named-2023-gartner-market-guide-email-security\"},{\"date\":\"Feb 8, 2023\",\"headline\":\"New Abnormal Security Research Shows Employees Open 28% of BEC Attacks, Fail to Report 98% of All Email Attacks\",\"summary\":\"The latest Abnormal research found that between July–December 2022, the median open rate for text-based business email compromise (BEC) attacks was nearly 28%.\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/h1-2023-threat-report\"},{\"date\":\"Jan 26, 2023\",\"headline\":\"Taking down the Hive ransomware gang\",\"summary\":\"The US Department of Justice says that a joint US and European operation has taken down the notorious Hive ransomware gang.\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/taking-down-the-hive-ransomware-gang\"},{\"date\":\"Nov 15, 2022\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal Security Redefines Cloud Email Security with the Launch of Security Posture Management to Protect Against Email Platform Attacks\",\"summary\":\"Abnormal Security announced today its newest addition to the product portfolio as the company progresses toward delivering the most comprehensive cloud email security in the market. The latest innovation protects customers from emerging email platform attacks that are increasing in volume and severity as attackers find new ways to target organizations.\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/redefines-cloud-email-security\"},{\"date\":\"Aug 10, 2022\",\"headline\":\"New Research Shows Rise in Credential Phishing Attacks with 265 Brands Impersonated in First Half of 2022\",\"summary\":\"Abnormal is recognized for its cloud-native email security platform that uses behavioral AI to analyze identity, content and context and leverages 45,000+ signals from cloud email platforms to stop all types of email attacks including business email compromise, supply chain fraud, ransomware, phishing, spam and graymail.\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/265-brands-impersonated-credential-phishing-attacks\"},{\"date\":\"Jun 29, 2022\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal Security Recognized as the Winner of 2022 Microsoft Rising Azure Technology Partner of the Year\",\"summary\":\"The Rising Azure Technology Partner of the Year Award recognizes a technology partner that has demonstrated strong customer focus and success by leveraging Microsoft Azure as their primary cloud platform.\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/microsoft-azure-rising-technology-partner\"},{\"date\":\"Jun 22, 2022\",\"headline\":\"New Trend in Business Email Compromise Emerges as Vendor Impersonation Overtakes CEO Fraud\",\"summary\":\"Abnormal is recognized for its cloud-native email security platform that uses behavioral AI to analyze identity, content and context and leverages 45,000+ signals from cloud email platforms to stop all types of email attacks including business email compromise, supply chain fraud, ransomware, phishing, spam and graymail.\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/shift-financial-supply-chain-compromise\"},{\"date\":\"Jun 2, 2022\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal Security Stops Email Attacks with Behavioral AI, Named to Forbes AI 50 for Third Consecutive Year\",\"summary\":\"Abnormal is recognized for its cloud-native email security platform that uses behavioral AI to analyze identity, content and context and leverages 45,000+ signals from cloud email platforms to stop all types of email attacks including business email compromise, supply chain fraud, ransomware, phishing, spam and graymail.\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/forbes-ai-50-2022\"},{\"date\":\"May 10, 2022\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal Security Raises $200M+ at a $4B Valuation To Protect The Modern Enterprise Workforce, With Its AI-based Email Security Platform\",\"summary\":\"Abnormal Security announced today the close of a $210 million Series C round of financing led by global software investor Insight Partners, with participation from Greylock Partners and Menlo Ventures. With this round, the 4-year-old company is now valued at $4 billion.\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/series-c-funding-4b-valuation\"},{\"date\":\"May 9, 2022\",\"headline\":\"Kim Sanchez from Abnormal Security Named on CRN’s 2022 Women of the Channel List\",\"summary\":\"Abnormal Security today announced that CRN®, a brand of The Channel Company, has named Kim Sanchez, Senior Channel Manager, to its Women of the Channel list for 2022.\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/crn-women-channel-2022\"},{\"date\":\"Aug 30, 2021\",\"headline\":\"Brute Force Email Attacks and Account Takeover Attempts Rise 671%, Reaching Unprecedented Levels, According to Abnormal Security Research\",\"summary\":\"Over the course of the quarter, Abnormal researchers saw a significant increase in credential phishing, as well as brute force attacks, which are used to obtain personal information such as passwords, passphrases and usernames through a string of continuous, automated attempts. Once accessed, compromised accounts can be leveraged to send additional attacks on coworkers, partners and vendors, and provide the credentials necessary to infiltrate other parts of the organization.\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/brute-force-email-attacks-account-takeover-attempts-rise\"},{\"date\":\"Aug 24, 2021\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal Joins Microsoft Intelligent Security Association\",\"summary\":\"MISA is comprised of independent software vendors and managed security service providers that have integrated their solutions to help customers better defend themselves against cyber threats. The Abnormal AI threat detection engine integrates with the Azure Active Directory APIs listed above and then models the identity of both employees and external senders to create relationship graphs and analyze email content to detect BEC attacks.\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/abnormal-joins-microsoft-intelligent-security-association\"},{\"date\":\"Apr 21, 2021\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal Security Adds Fortune 500-level Security Leadership Experience with Appointment of Mike Britton as Chief Information Security Officer\",\"summary\":\"Former Global Chief Security \u0026amp; Privacy Officer at Alliance Data Brings Valuable Experience and Understanding of Large Enterprise Needs to Help Company Deliver Lasting Value to Customers\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/mike-britton-appointed-chief-information-security-officer\"},{\"date\":\"Apr 15, 2021\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal Security Selected as Top 10 Finalist for RSA Conference 2021 Innovation Sandbox Contest\",\"summary\":\"Abnormal Security today announced the company has been named one of 10 finalists for the RSA Conference 2021 Innovation Sandbox Contest for its breakthrough cloud-native email security platform that stops modern email attacks through behavioral data science. On Wednesday, May 19, Abnormal Security will present its email security platform to a panel of renowned industry judges.\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/selected-top-10-finalist-innovation-sandbox-contest-2021\"},{\"date\":\"Mar 10, 2021\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal Security Named to Fast Company’s Annual List of the World’s Most Innovative Companies for 2021\",\"summary\":\"Abnormal Security today announced its placement on Fast Company’s prestigious annual list of the World’s Most Innovative Companies for 2021 for its breakthrough cloud-native email security platform that stops modern email attacks through behavioral data science. The list honors the businesses that have not only found a way to be resilient in the past year, but also turned those challenges into impact-making processes.\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/named-fast-companys-list-most-innovative-companies-2021\"},{\"date\":\"Feb 18, 2021\",\"headline\":\"Risk of SolarWinds-Style Attacks Through Vendor Email Compromise Increased 82%, Abnormal Threat Research Report Reveals\",\"summary\":\"Abnormal Security, a next-generation cloud email security company, today released a new threat research report that reveals an 82% increase in the chance of companies getting attacked through SolarWinds-style vendor email compromise (VEC) during any given week\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/risk-solarwinds-style-attacks-vendor-email-compromise-increased\"},{\"date\":\"Nov 19, 2020\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal Security Raises $50M in Series B Funding\",\"summary\":\"Abnormal Security, a next-generation email security company, today announced that it raised $50 million in Series B venture capital funding. Led by Menlo Ventures, with participation from early investor Greylock, the round brings Abnormal’s total funding to $75 million.\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/50m-series-b-funding\"},{\"date\":\"Oct 30, 2020\",\"headline\":\"Business Email Compromise (BEC) Attacks Rise in 75% of Industries According to Abnormal Security Research\",\"summary\":\"The research, which analyzes business email compromise attacks tracked by Abnormal from July-September 2020, found that BEC campaign volume increased 15% quarter-over-quarter, driven by an explosion in invoice and payment fraud.\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/q3-2020-report-bec-rises\"},{\"date\":\"Sep 15, 2020\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal Security and Microsoft Team up to Deliver AI-Driven Security\",\"summary\":\"Abnormal Security, a leader in protecting large enterprises from cybersecurity attacks, announced a global strategic alliance with Microsoft to deliver comprehensive security solutions to enterprises.\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/abnormal-microsoft-team-deliver-ai-driven-security\"},{\"date\":\"Aug 20, 2020\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal Security Quarterly BEC Report Shows How COVID-19 Zeitgeist Permeates Email Cyberattacks on Businesses\",\"summary\":\"Trends in BEC and email security during Q2 2020 included a peaking and plateauing of COVID-19-themed email attacks, an increase in BEC attack volume and acceleration of payment and invoice fraud. The report also reveals that Zoom supplanted American Express as the most impersonated brand in email attacks.\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/bec-report-covid-19-permeates-email-cyberattacks\"},{\"date\":\"Jun 30, 2020\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal Security Data Reveals 200 Percent Monthly Increase in Invoice and Payment Fraud Business Email Compromise Attacks\",\"summary\":\"Abnormal Securitytoday published research data that shows a 200 percent increase in BEC attacks focused on invoice or payment fraud from April to May 2020. This sharp rise continues the trend observed by Abnormal Security throughout the year.\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/200-percent-monthly-increase-invoice-payment-fraud\"},{\"date\":\"Jun 17, 2020\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal Security Issues Quarterly Business Email Compromise (BEC) Report for Q1 2020\",\"summary\":\"The first in a series of quarterly reports, the Q1 2020 report illustrates trends from actual BEC attacks discovered by Abnormal Security to help inform enterprise security strategy. The report also features a special section on email account compromise and security attack patterns during the COVID-19 pandemic.\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/business-email-compromise-report-q1-2020\"},{\"date\":\"May 21, 2020\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal Security Enhances Detection of Business Email Compromise (BEC) Attacks in Cloud Email Security Platform\",\"summary\":\"Abnormal Security, a leader in protecting large enterprises from Business Email Compromise (BEC) attacks, today introduced VendorBase, a global, federated database that tracks the reputations of an organization’s vendors and customers, and improves detection accuracy of advanced social engineering attacks.\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/enhanced-detection-business-email-compromise-cloud-security\"},{\"date\":\"May 7, 2020\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal Security Named a 2020 Cool Vendor in Cloud Office Security by Gartner\",\"summary\":\"Abnormal Security, a leader in protecting large enterprises from business email compromise (BEC) attacks, today announced it has been included in the list of Cool Vendors in Cloud Office Security by Gartner. The report recognizes vendors with “innovative approaches to cloud office security, email and collaboration.”\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/named-2020-cool-vendor-cloud-office-security-gartner\"},{\"date\":\"Apr 27, 2020\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal Security Appoints Kevin Moore as Chief Revenue Officer to Help Accelerate Company Growth\",\"summary\":\"Abnormal Security today announced the appointment of Kevin Moore as Chief Revenue Officer. With over 20 years of success leading high-performing global sales teams in the security industry, Kevin is responsible for scaling Abnormal’s worldwide sales team, operations and go-to-market engine.\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/kevin-moore-appointed-chief-revenue-officer\"},{\"date\":\"Apr 23, 2020\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal Security Protects Remote Workforces from Social Engineering Attacks With New Cloud Email Security integrations\",\"summary\":\"Abnormal Security announced the availability of Microsoft Teams protection and integration with Okta to extend email security coverage and protect remote workforces from social engineering attacks. Seamlessly delivered through Abnormal Security’s API-based integration with Office 365 and Okta’s Identity Cloud, respectively, these new integrations give enterprises more visibility, extended protection, and faster response to email-borne attacks.\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/new-cloud-email-security-integrations\"},{\"date\":\"Mar 13, 2020\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal Security Announces Completion of SOC 2 Type 2 Examination\",\"summary\":\"Abnormal Security, a leader in protecting large enterprises from Business Email Compromise (BEC) attacks, today announced completion of the Service Organization Control (SOC 2) examination. Conducted by Coalfire Controls, LLC, a fully licensed, accredited CPA firm and affiliate of Coalfire Systems, Inc, the voluntary examination confirms Abnormal Security’s commitment to inscrutable operating effectiveness.\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/announcing-completion-soc-2-type-2-examination\"},{\"date\":\"Dec 12, 2019\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal Security Appoints Rami Habal to Chief Product Officer\",\"summary\":\"Abnormal Security, the platform that protects large enterprises from the most sophisticated, targeted email attacks, today announced the appointment of Rami Habal to Chief Product Officer. Habal joins Abnormal following the company’s $24M Series A funding led by Greylock Partners and the general availability of its cloud email security platform.\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/rami-habal-appointed-chief-product-officer\"},{\"date\":\"Nov 20, 2019\",\"headline\":\"Abnormal Security Launches with $24M Series A Funding from Greylock to Protect Enterprises from Targeted Email Attacks\",\"summary\":\"\",\"href\":\"/newsroom/press-releases/launching-24m-series-a-funding-from-greylock\"}]}]\n"])</script></body></html>